---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageBackdrop from "../../components/PageBackdrop.astro";
import portrait from "../../assets/people/daniel-fokker.jpg";
import { inLang, sortByOrder } from "../../i18n/utils";

const all = await getCollection("cases");
const cases = sortByOrder(inLang(all, "en"));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Orbis Neo"
  description="About Daniel Fokker and Orbis Neo. Twenty-five years in the domains AI is now changing most."
  lang="en"
>
  <PageBackdrop flip />
  <section class="about container">
    <header class="about__header">
      <div class="about__intro">
        <h1>About Daniel Fokker and Orbis Neo</h1>
        <p class="about__lead">
          Good choices start with a clear picture of the facts. I map the complexity in your organisation, translate it into an executable plan and help carry it out. We agree up front how we will measure cost and impact.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="about__portrait">
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt="Daniel Fokker"
          widths={[280, 420, 560]}
          sizes="(max-width: 767px) 60vw, 420px"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </figure>
    </header>

    <section class="about__block">
      <h2>Why my background is relevant right now</h2>
      <h3>A combination that grew over time</h3>
      <p>I’ve spent twenty-five years working in the areas that AI is now disrupting most: IT delivery and software development, IT operations and management, enterprise architecture, HR, and IT financial management. The combination grew because each step in my career led me to an adjacent challenge.</p>
      <p>This combination helps leadership teams of mid-market and larger companies right now, because AI affects several domains at once. You need someone who sees how the pieces fit together: how a choice in IT operations ripples through into financial management, how an AI platform in delivery affects HR policy and how architecture decisions made today shape your room to manoeuvre later.</p>
      <p>Enterprise architecture is the thread running through my work. The discipline looks across domains by design, so I can help one area adapt while keeping an eye on the whole as your organisation changes.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about__block">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <h3>Interim and part-time, always with an endpoint</h3>
      <p>I work as an independent adviser through Orbis Neo. My preferred way of working is interim or part-time: senior support for an agreed period, with a clear endpoint and a handover to an internal owner.</p>
      <p>That fits my clients. Leadership teams of mid-market and larger companies want an adviser who understands their situation and structures that hold up after I leave. That is what my work is aimed at.</p>
      <p>For specific depth or extra capacity, I work with a network of professionals I bring in when needed.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about__block">
      <h2>Full career</h2>
      <ol class="about__cases">
        {cases.map((c) => (
          <li class="about-case">
            <p class="about-case__period">{c.data.period}</p>
            <h3>{c.data.role}</h3>
            <p class="about-case__org">{c.data.org}</p>
            <dl>
              <dt>Situation</dt>
              <dd>{c.data.situation}</dd>
              {c.data.result?.trim() && (
                <>
                  <dt>{c.data.ongoing ? "Mandate and progress" : "Result"}</dt>
                  <dd>{c.data.result}</dd>
                </>
              )}
            </dl>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="about__block">
      <h2>Education and knowledge</h2>
      <ul class="about__list">
        <li>MSc Business Administration, Radboud University (2013–2017)</li>
        <li>BSc Business Informatics, Avans (1999–2002)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Relevant knowledge and certifications: TOGAF, ArchiMate, IT4IT, TBM/IT Financial Management, PRINCE2, SAFe/Agile/Scrum, Lean Six Sigma.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about__block">
      <h2>About the name: Orbis Neo</h2>
      <p>
        Orbis Neo comes from Latin and literally means ‘new circle’ or ‘new world’. The name fits what I do: helping organisations in the middle of a technological shift make the way they are run workable again. The circle in the logo stands for completeness and coherence: keeping sight of the whole while its parts are in motion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about__block about__block--cta">
      <h2>Would you like to connect?</h2>
      <p>A first conversation takes fifteen minutes. After that, we'll both know whether a follow-up conversation makes sense.</p>
      <p><a href="/contact/" class="btn">Request an introductory call →</a></p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--page-head-pt) var(--section-y-compact);
  }

  .about__header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7fr 5fr;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  .about__lead {
    font-size: var(--fs-lead);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
  }

  .about__portrait {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about__portrait :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 420px;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  /* Full content width: heading left, text right (like the homepage segments). */
  .about__block {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
    column-gap: var(--space-7);
  }

  .about__block > h2 {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 1 / span 12;
    align-self: start;
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-h-compact) + var(--space-4));
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about__block > :not(h2) {
    grid-column: 2;
    max-width: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1023.98px) {
    .about__block {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about__block > h2 {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: auto;
      position: static;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }

    .about__block > :not(h2) {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }

  .about__cases {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: case;
    max-width: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .about-case {
    counter-increment: case;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    position: relative;
  }

  .about-case::before {
    content: counter(case);
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--space-5);
    right: var(--space-5);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--color-neo);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .about-case__period {
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .about-case__org {
    color: var(--color-action);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-case dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-case dt {
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  .about-case dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about__list {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  .about__block--cta > h2 {
    position: static;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about__block--cta {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-9);
    padding: var(--space-7);
    background: var(--color-surface-warm);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border-top: 0;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    padding: 14px 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    text-decoration: none;
    background: var(--color-action);
    color: #fff;
    min-height: 44px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767.98px) {
    .about__header {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about__portrait {
      order: -1;
    }

    .about__portrait :global(img) {
      max-width: 240px;
    }
  }
</style>
